     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear all,<div>I was analyzing data (published) from a colleague in order to test MSstats and after running a script I realized that the main protein of interest is missing. It is being filtered out at the beginnig:</div><div><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">quant </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">MaxQtoMSstatsFormat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">evidence</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">infile</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> annotation</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">annot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> proteinGroups</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">proteinGroups</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>                             proteinID</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;proteinGroups&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                             removeProtein_with1Peptide</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><div><br></div></div><div>This protein was identified in all samples with over 120 MS/MS counts, MaxQuant score of 255 and is highly abundant.</div><div><br></div><div>After running the commands:</div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">proteinGroups </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> read</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">table</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;proteinGroups.txt&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sep </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;\\t&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> header </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>infile </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> read</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">table</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;evidence.txt&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sep </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;\\t&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> header </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>annot </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> read</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">csv</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;maxquant_annotation.txt&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sep </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;\\t&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> header </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><div><br></div></div><div><b>proteinGroups </b>matrix has it, <b>ifile </b>has it with 121 entries and then in <b>quant </b>it&#39;s not there. </div><div>It&#39;s not a contaminant, it&#39;s not identified by site only and not a reverse of course. Any other analysis pipelines do not filter out this protein. </div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;d be happy for any help from your side. </div><div>Greetings</div><div>Witek </div><div><br></div></div>"
